-- title:
--   Full Slice Closeness Of IP CAB H Eval Sqrt
-- statement:
--   **Evaluated-slice commutation estimate from the processed-$G$ relation.**
--
--   Let $S$ be a symmetric strategy on the $(m+1)$-dimensional test space with normalized state $\psi$, and let $G^x$ be the indexed family of slice projective measurements. Sample an evaluated-slice question $q$, consisting of two ambient points, uniformly. Assume the two evaluated full-slice product families satisfy the state-dependent squared operator-distance relation with error
--
--   $$
--   \nu=48m\left(\gamma^{1/2}+\zeta^{1/2}\right).
--   $$
--
--   The normalization hypothesis is the one used to bound the evaluated product family. Then the difference between the evaluated cubic average and the evaluated quartic average is bounded by
--
--   $$
--   \left|\operatorname{evaluatedSliceABAAvg}(S,G)-\operatorname{evaluatedSliceABABAvg}(S,G)\right|\le \sqrt{\nu}.
--   $$
--
--   Here the two averages are the uniform evaluated-slice averages with their outcome sums, and the displayed error is the definition `commDataProcessedGError` evaluated at $(\gamma,\zeta)$. This scalar estimate is the evaluated-side input to the full-slice transport lemma.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Commutativity.fullSlice_closenessOfIP_CAB_hEval_sqrt`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
